{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/distances"]}],"metadata":{"title":"Distances","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"Distances"}],"role":"collection","externalID":"Distances","roleHeading":"Framework"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Distances\/documentation\/Distances\/Eccentricities"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Distances\/documentation\/Distances\/GraphProtocols"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Extended-Modules"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Distances\/documentation\/Distances","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"references":{"doc://Distances/documentation/Distances/Eccentricities":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every vertex’s eccentricity, computed once (Boost’s "},{"code":"all_eccentricities","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), with the measures"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that follow from them: the radius (the least), the diameter (the greatest), the center and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the periphery (the vertices that attain them). An eccentricity is "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", standing for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"infinity, when some vertex is not reachable from the vertex; so the diameter is "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" exactly"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when the graph is not connected (or not strongly connected), and the radius when no vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reaches every vertex."}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Eccentricities","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/distances\/eccentricities","identifier":"doc:\